g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">3-4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">lb</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Beef roast (ribeye or sirloin)</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tbsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Olive oil</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cloves</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Garlic (minced)</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Fresh rosemary (chopped)</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Fresh thyme (chopped)</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Salt</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">½</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Black pepper</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-9200-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"9200\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 roasting pan&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For placing the beef roast.</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 rack&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">To elevate the roast for even cooking.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-9200-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-9200-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"9200\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9200-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Preheat the Oven &#8211; Start by preheating your oven to 375°F. This is the perfect temperature for roasting beef to juicy perfection!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9200-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Prepare the Beef &#8211; Pat the beef roast dry with paper towels. This helps the seasoning stick better and gives you a nice crust.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9200-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Season the Roast &#8211; Rub all sides of the roast with olive oil. In a small bowl, mix together minced garlic, chopped rosemary, thyme, salt, and pepper. Press this flavorful mixture onto the surface of the roast.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9200-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Roast the Beef &#8211; Place the seasoned roast on a rack in a roasting pan. Roast in the preheated oven for about 20 minutes per pound for medium-rare. Adjust the time if you prefer it more or less done.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9200-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Rest and Serve &#8211; Once done, remove the roast from the oven and let it rest for 15 minutes. This allows the juices to redistribute. Slice thinly against the grain and serve warm. Enjoy your delicious roasted beef!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-9200-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>350</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>20g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>30g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>0g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these simple ingredients for a delicious<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roast_beef\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> roasted beef</a> that will impress everyone!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Roasted-Beef-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"Fresh ingredients for roasted beef displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-9198\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Roasted-Beef-Preparation.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Roasted-Beef-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Beef roast</strong> – 3-4 lb (ribeye or sirloin)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Olive oil</strong> – 2 tbsp</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Garlic</strong> – 4 cloves (minced)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Fresh rosemary</strong> – 1 tsp (chopped)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Fresh thyme</strong> – 1 tsp (chopped)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Salt</strong> – 1 tsp</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Black pepper</strong> – ½ tsp</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-roasted-beef\"><strong>How to Make Roasted Beef</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This delicious roasted beef recipe is perfect for any occasion! With a preparation time of 15 minutes, cooking time of about 1 hour and 40 minutes, and an additional resting time of 15 minutes, you&#8217;ll have a juicy and tender roast ready to impress your family and friends.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Roasted-Beef-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"Four-step process of preparing roasted beef, including preheating the oven, drying the roast, seasoning it, and roasting in the oven.\" class=\"wp-image-9199\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Roasted-Beef-Preparation.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Roasted-Beef-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Preheat the Oven</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Start by preheating your oven to 375°F. This is the perfect temperature for roasting beef to juicy perfection!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Prepare the Beef</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Pat the beef roast dry with paper towels. This helps the seasoning stick better and gives you a nice crust.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Season the Roast</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Rub all sides of the roast with olive oil. In a small bowl, mix together minced garlic, chopped rosemary, thyme, salt, and pepper. Press this flavorful mixture onto the surface of the roast.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Roast the Beef</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Place the seasoned roast on a rack in a roasting pan. Roast in the preheated oven for about 20 minutes per pound for medium-rare. Adjust the time if you prefer it more or less done.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Rest and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Once done, remove the roast from the oven and let it rest for 15 minutes. This allows the juices to redistribute. Slice thinly against the grain and serve warm. Enjoy your delicious roasted beef!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Main Course</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>100 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>15 minutes (resting)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>130 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>High Protein</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Warm, sliced against the grain</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-roasted-beef\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Roasted beef</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Let the beef come to room temperature before roasting for even cooking.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Season generously with salt and pepper to enhance flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use a meat thermometer to ensure perfect doneness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rest the beef after cooking to lock in juices.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with herbs like rosemary or thyme for added aroma.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-roasted-beef\"><strong>How to Serve this Roasted beef</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Slice it thin and serve on a crusty baguette for a delicious sandwich.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with creamy mashed potatoes and steamed green beans for a classic meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top a fresh salad with warm slices of roasted beef and a tangy vinaigrette.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with roasted vegetables for a colorful and nutritious side.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Make beef tacos using shredded roasted beef, topped with fresh salsa and avocado.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy it cold in a wrap with lettuce, tomatoes, and a zesty dressing.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing and enjoying your roasted beef leftovers is easy!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Roasted beef Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow the beef to cool to room temperature.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap tightly in plastic wrap or aluminum foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in an airtight container for extra protection.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3-4 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing Roasted beef</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Slice the beef into portions for easier thawing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap each portion in plastic wrap, then in foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and type of beef.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze for up to 3 months for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating Roasted beef</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight before reheating.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Preheat the oven to 325°F (165°C).</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place beef in a baking dish with a splash of broth or water.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cover with foil and heat for about 20-30 minutes until warmed through.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. How to make the perfect roast beef?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To make the perfect roast beef, start by selecting a good cut of beef, such as a ribeye or sirloin. Season it generously with salt and pepper, and let it come to room temperature before roasting. Preheat your oven to a high temperature, sear the beef on all sides in a hot skillet, then transfer it to the oven to finish cooking. Use a meat thermometer to check for doneness, and let it rest before slicing to ensure juiciness.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What cut of beef is used for roast beef?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Common cuts for roast beef include ribeye, sirloin, and tenderloin. Ribeye is known for its marbling and flavor, while sirloin is leaner and more affordable. Tenderloin is the most tender cut but can be pricier. Choose based on your preference for flavor and tenderness, and don’t forget to ask your butcher for recommendations!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What is the best way to season roast beef?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The best way to season roast beef is to keep it simple. A generous amount of salt and freshly cracked black pepper is often all you need. You can also add garlic powder, onion powder, or fresh herbs like rosemary and thyme for extra flavor. Rub the seasoning all over the meat and let it sit for at least 30 minutes before cooking to enhance the taste.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. How is roast beef done?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Roast beef is done when it reaches the desired internal temperature. For medium-rare, aim for about 135°F (57°C), while medium is around 145°F (63°C). Use a meat thermometer to check the temperature in the thickest part of the meat. Remember to let it rest for at least 15 minutes after cooking; this allows the juices to redistribute, making for a more tender and flavorful roast.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">There you have it, a delightful roasted beef recipe that’s as easy as pie! Picture the aroma filling your kitchen and the smiles around the table as you serve this juicy, tender dish. It’s perfect for family gatherings or a cozy dinner. So roll up your sleeves, enjoy the process, and savor every bite—you deserve it!</p>\n",
